      "body": "## Purpose\n\n`selective_state_update` picks its Triton launch config from a per-device JSON\nkeyed on `(headdim, dstate, device_name, cache_dtype)`. #50534 added that\nlookup and shipped configs for Intel Arc Pro B70. Intel Arc Pro B60 has no\nentry, so every B60 run falls back to the heuristic.\n\nThis PR adds the missing B60 files. No code changes.\n\n## Changes\n\nEight config files under\n`vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/ops/configs/selective_state_update/`, one\nper `(shape, cache_dtype)` pair, across four `(headdim, dstate)` shapes:\n\n- `headdim=64, dstate=128` — float16 and float32 (Mamba2 family, Zamba2-1.2B,\n  Nemotron-H-8B, Granite-4.0-h-tiny, Falcon-H1-0.5B)\n- `headdim=128, dstate=256` — float16 and float32 (Falcon-H1-3B/7B/34B)\n- `headdim=64, dstate=64` — float16 and float32 (Zamba2-2.7B)\n- `headdim=64, dstate=256` — float16 and float32 (Falcon-H1-1.5B(-Deep))\n\nThe first two shapes are the same ones the B70 PR shipped, so the two devices\nare directly comparable; the latter two cover Zamba2 and Falcon-H1 checkpoints\nthe B70 PR did not exercise.\n\n## Method\n\nGenerated on a single Intel Arc Pro B60 (23.91 GiB) with the in-tree\n`benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_selective_state_update.py --save-configs`,\nsweeping effective batch 8..131072, on vLLM 0.28.0 / torch 2.13.0+xpu.\n\n### Triton version\n\nAll eight files record `\"triton_version\": \"3.8.0\"`. They were first tuned on\nTriton 3.7.x, then re-checked on Triton 3.8.0 (torch 2.14.0+xpu, one B60 per\nshape, tune and cross-eval in the same pod). Seven shapes keep their winners:\nthe shipped config is within 1.006-1.036x geomean of the best re-measured one.\n`headdim=64, dstate=128, float16` moved on 3.8.0 (shipped config 1.10x geomean,\nup to 1.99x slower at small batch), so that file now holds the 3.8.0 winners for\neffective batch 8..32768 and keeps the 65536/131072 entries from the original\nsweep. The end-to-end numbers below were measured with the Triton 3.7.x configs\nand not repeated on 3.8.0.\n\n## Results\n\n### Numerical validation\n\nEvery shipped config (all 8 shape/cache_dtype combinations) was validated\nagainst the fp32 reference (`--validate`) across the capped batch grid\n8..2048 (9 points) — all 72 checks passed.\n\n### Kernel speedup\n\nHeuristic vs. tuned, `--compare`, on the first two (B70-comparable) shapes:\n\n| shape | cache_dtype | geomean | min | max |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| headdim=64, dstate=128 | float16 | 3.36x | 1.42x | 4.91x |\n| headdim=64, dstate=128 | float32 | 2.68x | 1.26x | 6.38x |\n| headdim=128, dstate=256 | float16 | 6.12x | 3.73x | 10.26x |\n| headdim=128, dstate=256 | float32 | 3.83x | 3.05x | 7.27x |\n\nOverall geomean **3.71x** across 54 (shape, cache_dtype, batch) entries; every\nsingle entry improves over the heuristic.\n\n### End-to-end\n\n`vllm serve` + `vllm bench serve`, 512 in / 128 out, 32 prompts, paired by rep,\narms alternating base/tuned within each rep. Base is the pristine package (no\nB60 file present); tuned installs the configs above.\n\n| model | shape | base tok/s | tuned tok/s | speedup | reps won |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Zyphra/Zamba2-1.2B-instruct (run 1) | 64,128 | 490.05 | 568.08 | +15.92% | 6/6 |\n| Zyphra/Zamba2-1.2B-instruct (run 2) | 64,128 | 500.00 | 658.53 | +31.71% | 6/6 |\n| Zyphra/Zamba2-2.7B-instruct | 64,64 | 133.47 | 136.16 | +2.02% | 6/6 |\n| tiiuae/Falcon-H1-3B-Instruct | 128,256 | 296.51 | 651.06 | +119.57% | 6/6 |\n| tiiuae/Falcon-H1-1.5B-Instruct | 64,256 | 504.41 | 780.34 | +54.70% | 6/6 |\n\nAll five runs are significant under a paired permutation test (p=0.0321, the\nsmallest a 6-pair test can report), and tuned wins every rep in every run.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Regenerate with `benchmark_selective_state_update.py --save-configs` on B60\n  and confirm the same winners.\n- `--validate` every shipped key; a failing config is dropped, not shipped.\n- Serve a Mamba2/Zamba2/Falcon-H1 model on B60 and confirm the tuned file is\n  the one loaded.\n- No CUDA/ROCm behaviour changes: this PR is data only.\n\n",
      "changedFiles": 8,
